        "uuid": "3bbc3a5f_9131ffa7",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/shader_io.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T21:05:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From GLSLang, I don\u0027t think so? From my reading of teh docs, I believ `gl_PerVertex` is special, it isn\u0027t really a struct in GLSL, as you access the members directly `gl_Position`, etc. So, gl_PerVertex is just, like, a holder? of things that get accessed in other ways.\n\n\u003e gl_PerVertex defines an interface block for outputs. The block is defined without an instance name, so that prefixing the names is not required.\n\u003e \n\u003e https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Built-in_Variable_(GLSL)",
      "parentUuid": "c57422e4_f2e92d28",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3544c035_25d4dd67",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/shader_io.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T22:54:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that the old SPIR-V reader does not support this and asserts if it happens. We should probably do the same, otherwise users might be surprised (since this is not a SPIR-V restriction, some non-glslang tools might do it).\n\nAlso, the `PointSize` member *will* be accessed (to assign 1.0), so this isn\u0027t really the right logic anyway. We should instead just always skip both `CullDistance` and `PointSize`. We can assert that `CullDistance` is not accessed using `IsIndexAccessed()`, but I don\u0027t think we should make decisions using it.",
      "parentUuid": "3bbc3a5f_9131ffa7",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "583f99b9_0f07a6f7",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/shader_io.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T21:38:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m confused. What is the issue that you\u0027d like me to assert on? If the `gl_PerVertex` struct is copied?\n\nThe `PointSize` will already work if it is assigned, there will be an index access so we\u0027d emit the assignment to the struct. Otherwise, we\u0027ll need ot find that access and delete it and any usages? The AST reader recorded the point size member index. It didnt\u0027 record for clip or cull distances.\n\nI\u0027ve re-written the code slightly, asserting for CullDistance if used, but if there is something else you\u0027d like changed, please let me know as I\u0027m not sure what else is desired here at the moment.",
      "parentUuid": "3544c035_25d4dd67",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94203b8a_3e99a5a9",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/shader_io.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-10T18:45:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What is the issue that you\u0027d like me to assert on? If the gl_PerVertex struct is copied?\n\nI think we could probably just reject if any of the uses are not `access`?\n\n\n\u003e The PointSize will already work if it is assigned, there will be an index access so we\u0027d emit the assignment to the struct.\n\nThe issue is that if `PointSize` is accessed then you still emit a `@builtin(__point_size)` member (tested this locally with handwritten SPIR-V, but a unit test should show it too). So we need to always skip it, and just check that it was assigned instead.",
      "parentUuid": "583f99b9_0f07a6f7",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11cf6ef8_0ad7f8cd",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/shader_io.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-12T01:30:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure if we shoudl reject if any use is not an access. We don\u0027t actually know this is `gl_PerVertex` we just see a struct with stuff in it. We can skip emitting that suff if we don\u0027t understand it, but I don\u0027t think we should necessarily drop the struct for other uses?\n\nI\u0027ve skipped emission of PointSize and left a TODO for adding a check that the only usage of that member is an assignment.",
      "parentUuid": "94203b8a_3e99a5a9",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1a009f9_8c2bcb64",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/reader/lower/shader_io.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 288,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T14:43:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think the logic should be:\n\"if any of the members were skipped, then reject if any uses of the var are not `access`\"\n\nBecause if there are any skipped members, we can only support direct member access on the other members. Any whole-struct uses will not be handled correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "11cf6ef8_0ad7f8cd",
      "revId": "f1c28fe8671ffba7ea7b5411b6ed0615a140d9b2",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
